<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rivonia Trial</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1963–1964</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rivonia Trial was held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> in 1963–1964 against leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> and its armed wing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umkhonto-we-sizwe">Umkhonto we Sizwe</a>, after a police raid on their hideout at Liliesleaf Farm in Rivonia, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a> used his statement from the dock to defend the armed struggle. In June 1964 he and seven others were convicted of sabotage and sentenced to life imprisonment.</p></div>
